/-!
# Integer data for doubled D4 root factorizations

The 192 entries are candidate simple words and their matrices in integral
simple-coroot coordinates. Each path entry records a positive root, the index
of the remaining product, and an integral displacement witness. `Checks`
certifies all arithmetic; `Factorizations` identifies the entries with the
actual Weyl group and proves coverage. These definitions alone assert no
classification or factorization theorem.

The small tables were generated from the preserved diagnostic witnesses in
`Source/factorizations.json`; see `Source/README.md`. The proof uses only
kernel-checked integer calculations, not the generator's correctness.

Source: the D4 specialization supporting Steinberg, §§4–6 and 8.2(6)–(7),
`refs/KGroup/GLS3/Chapter2St2.tex`.
-/

